00:12:22.950 --> 00:12:25.400
You already made it, or
may be also in another role

00:12:25.400 --> 00:12:28.010
in industry, another high-paced career.

00:12:28.010 --> 00:12:29.700
And now of course, you
don't just wanna make

00:12:29.700 --> 00:12:32.920
a solid a good job, but you
really wanna make a great job.

00:12:32.920 --> 00:12:33.850
Do you wanna be successful?

00:12:33.850 --> 00:12:35.200
You really wanna do your best.

00:12:35.200 --> 00:12:36.660
So from your perspective,

00:12:36.660 --> 00:12:39.540
what distinguishes a good consultant

00:12:39.540 --> 00:12:41.940
from a great consultant?

00:12:41.940 --> 00:12:43.900
How are you really outstanding?

00:12:43.900 --> 00:12:45.180
What do you need to do?

00:12:45.180 --> 00:12:48.200
What distinguishes these
two types of provides?

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:50.750
- Yeah, so that's a question I often get

00:12:50.750 --> 00:12:54.870
as a coach for our people internally,

00:12:54.870 --> 00:12:57.650
where I take, let's say,
a career advisor role

00:12:57.650 --> 00:13:00.600
throughout a couple of years
for younger colleagues.

00:13:00.600 --> 00:13:03.540
And for me, one of the
most important topics here

00:13:03.540 --> 00:13:05.530
would be to be proactive.

00:13:05.530 --> 00:13:08.070
So not reacting on what
your project manager,

00:13:08.070 --> 00:13:09.650
the client demands or whatever,

00:13:09.650 --> 00:13:12.530
but always trying to think
one or two steps ahead,

00:13:12.530 --> 00:13:13.730
what's happening next?

00:13:13.730 --> 00:13:18.730
What do I need to prepare now
to make the project successful

00:13:19.210 --> 00:13:21.300
in the next step?

00:13:21.300 --> 00:13:26.300
And then secondly, also, an
advice I give very many people

00:13:26.649 --> 00:13:31.649
within our organization, is
also to think in solutions.

00:13:31.970 --> 00:13:35.550
So not come back in your project team,

00:13:35.550 --> 00:13:38.570
to your project manager, or
whatever, with a problem.

00:13:38.570 --> 00:13:40.330
It's great to ask questions.

00:13:40.330 --> 00:13:42.210
If you have a problem,
you should come back.

00:13:42.210 --> 00:13:44.680
But when you come back, I
expect the very good people

00:13:44.680 --> 00:13:48.700
always to have thought
through a different series,

00:13:48.700 --> 00:13:51.960
let's say, of solutions they might have.

00:13:51.960 --> 00:13:53.940
And they can still ask
me, "Is it the right one?"

00:13:53.940 --> 00:13:55.750
Maybe I have a totally different one.

00:13:55.750 --> 00:13:58.320
But if I see they thought
about it, they have

00:13:58.320 --> 00:14:02.460
some good first ideas,
then it's much more easier.

00:14:02.460 --> 00:14:05.200
And this is also making the difference

00:14:06.370 --> 00:14:07.800
to find the right solution.

00:14:07.800 --> 00:14:10.770
And not just here's my
problem, solve it for me.

